  "latestMilestone": "Canonical SWIR_OS main now includes PR #42 and PR #43. The official NVIDIA Debian 13 x86_64 qualification probe now pins the exact reviewed 40-hex primary signing-key fingerprint 02182E60104FCDC26EAE1B8597A5D4CB8793F200, requires the InRelease signature to bind to that primary key, and fails closed on missing, invalid, stale, expired or excessively future-dated signed metadata using a 14-day maximum age and 24-hour future-skew bound while honoring Valid-Until when present. The probe remains qualification-only and cannot enable repositories or authorize mutation. Driver Center CI was also corrected so deterministic safety/runtime contracts stay mandatory while hosted-runner PCI visibility is treated as environment evidence: zero-PCI runners no longer fabricate hardware or create false product failures, and the separate Hardware Live E2E remains the stronger live-environment gate. Post-merge checks for canonical commit be8873b0 passed. The authoritative roadmap remains 55/65 (84.6%) because vendor repository activation and journaled transaction/recovery E2E remain open. Live USB, installer and detached installed boot are VM-verified; physical USB qualification remains pending, with Secure Boot and legacy BIOS not claimed.",
